URL:https://calendar.phoenixpubliclibrary.org/event/17806186
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Día de los Muertos Celebration
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 2026 Día de los Muertos celebration at Burton 
 Barr Central Library as we honor the tradition of remembering family and 
 friends who have passed. This year’s Día de los Muertos exhibition is a 
 display of nichos created by local communities. Visit the community altar 
 to write messages to loved ones or bring a photo of a loved one to share on 
 the community *photo wall. Papel picado\, nichos\, and ofrendas will all be 
 included in this year's celebration on the 2nd floor. Search for clues in a 
 scavenger hunt that will lead to other displays around the library. Winners 
 collect a prize on the 5th floor!\n\nOn display from October 6 through 
 November 6\, 2026. Burton Barr Central Library\, 2nd floor by Arizona Room. 
 \n\n*Please leave wallet-sized\, 2 x 3 inch photocopies only. Photos will 
 not be returned at the end of the event. \n \n\nDo you require an 
 accommodation to participate in a Phoenix Public Library program\, 
 service\, or activity? Call 602-262-4636\, TTY 711\, or submit your request 
 in person or through Ask Us at least 14 business days before the 
 event.\n\n¿Necesita alguna adaptación para participar en algún 
 programa\, servicio o actividad de Phoenix Public Library? Llame al 
 602-262-4636\, a la línea TTY al 711 o presente una solicitud en persona o 
 por medio de Ask Us por lo menos 14 días hábiles antes del evento.\n
LOCATION:Burton Barr Central Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Alex Mada":MAILTO:alex.mada@phoenix.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts, Culture, Entertainment & Exhibits
UID:LibCal-15413-17436704
URL:https://calendar.phoenixpubliclibrary.org/event/17436704
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261017T170000Z
DTEND:20261017T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Family Storytime
DESCRIPTION:Who’s it for? Children\, birth to age five\, and their 
 favorite grownups \n\nWhat will you do? Play\, read\, sing\, and dance with 
 your children in a fun\, active program that builds reading skills. 
 \n\nWhat is your child learning? Children who love books and stories become 
 better readers. \n\nUnless posted\, this program is held every week at this 
 time. \n\nSupport for early literacy programs is provided by a grant from 
 First Things First\, which partners with families and communities to give 
 all Arizona children the opportunity to arrive at kindergarten healthy and 
 ready to succeed. Learn more at FirstThingsFirst.org.\n\n \n\nDo you 
 require an accommodation to participate in a Phoenix Public Library 
 program\, service\, or activity? Call 602-262-4636\, TTY 711\, or submit 
 your request in person or through Ask Us at least 14 business days before 
 the event.
LOCATION:MACH1\, Burton Barr Central Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Stephanie Stoner":MAILTO:stephanie.stoner@phoenix.gov
CATEGORIES:Childrens' Programs, Storytimes
UID:LibCal-15413-16986970
URL:https://calendar.phoenixpubliclibrary.org/event/16986970
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261017T220000Z
DTEND:20261018T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Dungeons and Dragons
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a game of Dungeons & Dragons in Teen Central! 
 Whether you're new to DnD\, or a skilled Dungeon Master\, all skill levels 
 are welcome. During this program players will have the chance to learn the 
 mechanics of Dungeons & Dragons and expand their DnD skill set. Have fun 
 building your own characters and running campaigns while exploring the 
 broader world of storytelling\, role playing and strategic game play. Every 
 Saturday at 3PM.\n\nDo you require an accommodation to participate in a 
 Phoenix Public Library program\, service\, or activity? Call 602-262-4636\, 
 TTY 711\, or submit your request in person or through Ask Us at least 14 
 business days before the event
LOCATION:Teen Central\, Burton Barr Central Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Jennifer Kause":MAILTO:jennifer.kause@phoenix.gov
CATEGORIES:STEAM, Teen Programs
UID:LibCal-15413-16479160
URL:https://calendar.phoenixpubliclibrary.org/event/16479160
END:VEVENT
