SUMMARY:Morning Circle Time
DESCRIPTION:Let’s get ready for school by having a morning circle time. 
 We will talk about the days of the week\, the events coming up\, ask fun\, 
 engaging questions and share new things with each other. After circle time 
 we will all go to storytime!   \n\nWe are Now Located on the 4th floor 
 next to MACH!\n \n\nFRC Programs are for children birth to 5 years old and 
 their caregivers.        \n\nSupport for the Phoenix Families 
 First Resource Center is provided by a grant from First Things 
 First.       \n\n  \n\nDo you require an accommodation to 
 participate in a Phoenix Public Library program\, service\, or activity? 
 Call 602-262-4636\, TTY 711\, or submit your request in person or through 
 Ask Us at least 14 business days before the event.   \n\n  
 \n\n¿Necesita alguna adaptación para participar en algún programa\, servicio o actividad de 
 Phoenix Public Library? Llame al 602-262-4636\, a la línea TTY al 
 711 o presente una solicitud en persona o por medio de Ask 
 Us por lo menos 14 días hábiles antes del evento
LOCATION:Lecture Room\, Burton Barr Central Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Casey Diaz":MAILTO:casey.diaz@phoenix.gov
