SUMMARY:Room on the Broom
DESCRIPTION:Bubble\, bubble\, toil\, and trouble! Join us for a magical 
 Halloween art activity where kids make a bubbling cauldron potion using 
 paint and cardboard tube stampers. Little witches and wizards will dip\, 
 stamp\, and splash bright colors to create fizzy\, bubbly potion circles 
 rising out of a cauldron. It’s messy\, colorful\, and full of Halloween 
 fun—every child will leave with their own enchanting bubbling brew 
 masterpiece! \n\n \n\nWe are Now Located on the 4th floor next to 
 MACH!\n\nFRC Programs are for children birth to 5 years old and their 
 caregivers.        \n\nSupport for the Phoenix Families First 
 Resource Center is provided by a grant from First Things 
 First.       \n\n\nDo you require an accommodation to 
 participate in a Phoenix Public Library program\, service\, or activity? 
 Call 602-262-4636\, TTY 711\, or submit your request in person or through 
 Ask Us at least 14 business days before the event.   
 \n\n¿Necesita alguna adaptación para participar en algún programa\, servicio o actividad de 
 Phoenix Public Library? Llame al 602-262-4636\, a la línea TTY al 
 711 o presente una solicitud en persona o por medio de Ask 
 Us por lo menos 14 días hábiles antes del evento
LOCATION:Lecture Room\, Burton Barr Central Library
